help-feedback = Help and Feedback
support-contact = Contact the developers
support-staff-queue = Support requests
support-new-request = New request
support-manage = Manage stored requests
support-delete = Delete this request permanently
support-purge-closed = Delete closed requests permanently
support-purge-all = Delete all requests and reset numbering
support-retention = Stored requests: { $total }, including { $closed } closed. Closing keeps a conversation available; deletion permanently removes it and its queued alerts. Existing database backups retain their own retention policy.
support-confirm-delete = Permanently delete request #{ $id }, “{ $subject }”, from user { $username }, including every message and queued alert? This cannot be undone in the support interface.
support-confirm-purge-closed = Permanently delete all { $count } closed requests, their messages, and their queued alerts? Gameplay will pause during deletion. Open requests and numbering are preserved. This cannot be undone in the support interface.
support-confirm-purge-all = Permanently delete all { $count } requests, including open conversations, every message, and all queued support alerts? Gameplay will pause during deletion. The next request will be numbered 1. This cannot be undone in the support interface.
database-maintenance-operation-support-purge = support request deletion
database-maintenance-support-purge-started = Support request storage maintenance has started. Gameplay and account changes are paused until it finishes.
database-maintenance-support-purge-completed = Support request storage maintenance has finished. Gameplay and account changes have resumed.
database-maintenance-support-purge-failed = Support request storage maintenance could not complete. Gameplay and account changes have resumed.
support-deleted = Request #{ $id }, its messages, and its queued alerts have been deleted.
support-purged-closed = Deleted { $count } closed requests, their messages, and their queued alerts.
support-purged-all = Deleted { $count } requests, all their messages, and all queued support alerts. The next request will be numbered 1.
support-purge-stale = The request collection changed after you opened the deletion prompt. Nothing was deleted. Review the updated count and confirm again if you still want to delete it.
support-delete-error = No requests were deleted because storage is temporarily unavailable. The confirmation is still here. Try Confirm again later, or cancel.
support-purge-temporary = Bulk deletion is unavailable for temporary server storage. No requests were deleted. You can delete individual requests instead.
support-intro = Send a private request to the developers. Replies are saved here for you to read when you return; this is not live chat. For abuse or misconduct, use Report user. Do not include passwords or reset codes.
support-category-accessibility = Accessibility, speech, and audio
support-category-game = Game rules or gameplay problem
support-category-account = Account or connection help
support-category-suggestion = Suggest an improvement
support-category-contact = Other question for the developers
support-filter-status = Status: { $value }
support-filter-scope = Requests: { $value }
support-filter-current = { $value } (selected)
support-scope-all = All users' requests
support-scope-mine = My requests
support-status-all = All statuses
support-status-open = Awaiting developer reply
support-status-waiting_user = Awaiting user reply
support-status-closed = Closed
support-list-count = Support requests in this view: { $count }.
support-ticket-row = Request #{ $id }: { $subject }. { $status }. Updated { $date }.
support-inbox-row = Request #{ $id } from { $username }: { $subject }. { $status }. Updated { $date }.
support-ticket-header = Request #{ $id }: { $subject }. Category: { $category }. Status: { $status }.
support-owner = Submitted by user { $username }.
support-author-staff = Developer
support-author-user = Request owner
support-message = { $author } ({ $username }), { $date }: { $message }
support-reply = Add a reply
support-close = Close this request
support-reopen = Reopen this request
support-prompt-subject = Briefly describe your issue (1–{ $limit } characters).
support-prompt-body = Describe your question or suggestion. For a problem, include what happened, what you expected, your device, and steps to reproduce (1–{ $limit } characters). Do not include passwords or reset codes.
support-prompt-reply = Write your reply (1–{ $limit } characters). Do not include passwords or reset codes.
support-confirm-action = Confirm
support-saved = Request #{ $id } has been saved.
support-unavailable = This support request is unavailable or you no longer have permission to view it. Return to Help and Feedback, Contact the developers.
support-invalid-text = Enter between 1 and { $limit } characters of plain text. The subject must be a single line. Your request has not been sent.
support-active-limit = The request owner already has { $limit } active requests. Continue an existing request or close one that is no longer needed before opening another. Your draft has not been sent.
support-daily-limit = You have created { $limit } requests in the past 24 hours. Continue an existing conversation or try again later. Your draft has not been sent.
support-hourly-limit = You have sent { $limit } conversation entries in the past hour. Wait before sending another. Your draft has not been sent.
support-conversation-limit = This conversation has reached its { $limit }-entry limit. You can close it and create a new request, referring to this request's number. Your draft has not been sent.
support-stale = This request changed while you were reading or writing. Your change was not sent. Choose Read the latest conversation to review the update, then review your pending change again before confirming.
support-closed-error = This request is closed. Reopen it before adding a reply.
support-notify-staff = Support requests awaiting the developers: { $count }. Open Help and Feedback, Contact the developers.
support-notify-user = You have updates on { $count } support requests. Open Help and Feedback, Contact the developers, and choose All statuses to read them.
support-notify-current = Request #{ $id } has an update. The conversation updates automatically; your reading position is preserved.
support-live-error = Conversation updates are temporarily unavailable. Your current view is still here; updates will resume automatically when storage recovers.
support-event-closed = Closed this request.
support-event-open = Reopened this request.
support-read-latest = Read the latest conversation
support-review-again = Keep my draft and review it again
support-review-deletion = Review deletion again
support-edit-subject = Edit subject
support-edit-body = Edit message
support-storage-error = Your change could not be saved because storage is temporarily unavailable. Your draft is still here. Try Confirm again later, or cancel.
support-read-error = Support requests could not be loaded right now. Return to Contact the developers and try again later.
support-draft-read-error = Your draft could not be reviewed because storage is temporarily unavailable. Your text is still in the input field. Try submitting it again later, or cancel.
support-confirm-create = Send the request “{ $subject }” to the developers? Review your message below. Cancel to discard it.
support-confirm-reply-team = Send this reply to the developers about request #{ $id }, “{ $subject }”? Review your message below.
support-confirm-reply-user = Send this developer reply to user { $username } about request #{ $id }, “{ $subject }”? Review your message below.
support-confirm-closed = Close request #{ $id }, “{ $subject }”? You can reopen it later if you need further help.
support-confirm-open = Reopen request #{ $id }, “{ $subject }”, and return it to the developers' queue?
